{"id": "narrative-01", "question": "What supply chain risks does Apple describe in its fiscal 2026 10-K?", "type": "narrative", "expected_answer": "Reliance on single or limited sources for critical components (advanced semiconductors, memory, storage); concentrated global supply chains exposed to geopolitical tension, conflict and instability; component shortages and rising costs", "sources": [{"company": "AAPL", "filing": "0000320193-26-000026", "form_type": "10-K", "fiscal_period": "FY2026 FY", "section": "item_1a", "page": 8, "chunk_id": "0000320193-26-000026:item_1a:2", "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/320193/000032019326000026/aapl-20260926.htm", "evidence": "relies on single or limited sources for critical components, such as advanced semiconductors, memory and storage"}], "verified": false}
{"id": "narrative-02", "question": "How did U.S. export controls on the H20 affect NVIDIA in fiscal year 2026?", "type": "narrative", "expected_answer": "In April 2025 the U.S. government required a license to export H20 to China and D:5 countries; NVIDIA took a $4.5 billion charge in Q1 fiscal 2026 for excess H20 inventory and purchase obligations; licenses granted in August 2025 produced only about $60 million of H20 revenue", "sources": [{"company": "NVDA", "filing": "0001045810-26-000021", "form_type": "10-K", "fiscal_period": "FY2026 FY", "section": "item_1a", "page": 26, "chunk_id": "0001045810-26-000021:item_1a:40", "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1045810/000104581026000021/nvda-20260125.htm", "evidence": "requires a license for export to China"}, {"company": "NVDA", "filing": "0001045810-26-000021", "form_type": "10-K", "fiscal_period": "FY2026 FY", "section": "item_1a", "page": 26, "chunk_id": "0001045810-26-000021:item_1a:41", "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1045810/000104581026000021/nvda-20260125.htm", "evidence": "we incurred a $4.5 billion charge in the first quarter of fiscal year 2026"}], "verified": false}
{"id": "narrative-03", "question": "What certification and production risks does Boeing describe for its new aircraft programs?", "type": "narrative", "expected_answer": "Programs such as the 777X, 737-7 and 737-10 have had significant delays; the FAA determines certification timing; planned 737 and 787 production rate increases may be delayed if safety KPIs do not support them or FAA concurrence is not obtained", "sources": [{"company": "BA", "filing": "0001628280-26-004357", "form_type": "10-K", "fiscal_period": "FY2025 FY", "section": "item_1a", "page": 9, "chunk_id": "0001628280-26-004357:item_1a:2", "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/12927/000162828026004357/ba-20251231.htm", "evidence": "the FAA ultimately determines the timing of certification"}, {"company": "BA", "filing": "0001628280-26-004357", "form_type": "10-K", "fiscal_period": "FY2025 FY", "section": "item_1a", "page": 9, "chunk_id": "0001628280-26-004357:item_1a:3", "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/12927/000162828026004357/ba-20251231.htm", "evidence": "unable to obtain FAA concurrence"}], "verified": false}
